    "text": "# Add to Dock in Safari\n\nRequires macOS Sonoma 14 or later. These illustrations show the File menu route; Safari also offers Add to Dock in its Share menu.\n\n1. **Open the *File* menu.** Open the website in Safari. In the menu bar at the top of your Mac screen, click File.\n2. **Choose *Add to Dock*.** In the File menu, click Add to Dock. Safari opens a confirmation dialog for this website.\n3. **Click *Add*.** Keep or edit the app name, then click Add. A web app is saved to your Applications folder and added to the Dock.\n"
